window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1c"]={"https://theconversation.com/when-it-comes-to-rape-cases-involving-a-celebrity-the-media-too-often-miss-the-point-296256":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"20c37d7fce963f4b84999a53bd6fafc8950ecd89c33328a0592c424bd9eec041","read":"https://theconversation.com/when-it-comes-to-rape-cases-involving-a-celebrity-the-media-too-often-miss-the-point-296256","bytes":178274,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"When it comes to rape cases involving a celebrity, the media too often miss the point","by":[{"n":"Jane Gilmore","r":"PhD candidate, Monash Gender and Family Violence Prevention Hub, Monash University"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T01:49:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Russell Brand has been convicted of one count of rape and three counts of sexual assault and sentenced to ten years and six months in prison."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Age","https://www.theage.com.au/search?isSemanticSearch=true&text=russell+brand"],", ",["The Herald Sun","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/search-results?q=russell%20brand"],", ",["The Guardian","https://www.google.co.uk/search?q=russell+brand&as_sitesearch=www.theguardian.com"],", ",["the ABC","https://www.abc.net.au/news/search?query=russell%20brand"]," and ",["The Australian","https://www.theaustralian.com.au/search-results?q=russell%20brand"]," all reported extensively on the trial, verdict and sentencing. While it’s certainly newsworthy that another public figure has finally been held to account for years of predatory behaviour, the nature of reporting on celebrity rape trials is worth examining."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the ",["UK’s Channel 4","https://www.channel4.com/news/debate-the-use-of-rape-myths-in-trials-must-be-challenged"]," reported, ",["rape myths","https://theconversation.com/rape-myths-shape-how-we-respond-to-sexual-violence-what-are-they-and-what-impact-do-they-have-292594"]," were a frequent and misleading feature in Brand’s trial."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Rape myths shape how we respond to sexual violence. What are they and what impact do they have?","https://theconversation.com/rape-myths-shape-how-we-respond-to-sexual-violence-what-are-they-and-what-impact-do-they-have-292594"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research","https://global.oup.com/academic/product/reforming-rape-trials-9780198948148?cc=au&lang=en&"]," in Australia has found rape myths are routinely relied on in rape trials, not only by defence lawyers, but also by prosecutors, judges, juries and police."]},{"k":"p","s":["One pervasive rape myth is the “ ",["monster myth","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/14791420.2020.1854802"],"”, the belief that rape is committed by monstrously deviant strangers who attack innocent young girls in public places. ",["Research","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/0963947012444217"]," shows this myth is prevalent in media reporting of rape, which has an impact on public perception and acceptance of the monster myth."]},{"k":"p","s":["In reality, as Australian Bureau of Statistics ",["data","https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/crime-and-justice/sexual-violence/2021-22#incident-characteristics"]," shows, the person most likely to rape a woman is a man who is her intimate partner."]},{"k":"h","s":["Rape myths in news media"]},{"k":"p","s":["In my research (which has not yet been peer reviewed) I used the AustLii database to identify 32 rape cases in the County Court of Victoria that resulted in a guilty outcome between July 2025 and August 2026. Two of those cases were the ",["Tom Silvagni trial","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-12-11/tom-silvagni-identified-as-man-found-guilty-of-rape/106129488"]," and the ",["Ralph Carr trial","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-08-25/ralph-carr-sentenced-to-six-years-jail-for-rape/107074230"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I also searched for news reporting on those trials, finding 198 articles that fit the inclusion criteria. Between them, Silvagni and Carr received 85% of the media coverage of the entire dataset."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rape myths were present in almost 45% of the headlines in the dataset. They appeared in more than 60% of the non-celebrity cases (almost entirely centred on the monster myth) and just over 40% of the celebrity cases (where the myths that women commonly lie about rape and that men charged with rape are an object of pity predominated). Every publication in the study included rape myths in some of their headlines about rape trials."]},{"k":"p","s":["In other words, if media are reporting on a celebrity trial, too often the celebrity becomes the story, not the rape or the victim-survivor."]},{"k":"p","s":["If they’re reporting on rape cases, the monster myth is more likely to appear in the headline than the facts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of the 32 cases I identified, 13 were cases of rape in a family and domestic violence (FDV) context. Less than 3% of the articles were about the cases involving rape in an FDV context."]},{"k":"p","s":["Journalists cannot identify the complainant (the legal term for the victim-survivor) in a rape trial, so if they report an FDV related rape case, they often cannot name the perpetrator because it can identify the victim-survivor."]},{"k":"p","s":["The courts often use pseudonyms for both people when they publish sentencing remarks. Journalists could report these cases using those pseudonyms, preserving the victim-survivor’s anonymity while still informing the public about the rape. I could not find a single article in my dataset that did this."]},{"k":"p","s":["Focusing such breathless attention on celebrity cases and the rare stranger-danger rape endorses exactly the kind of monster myths that ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/news/2026/nov/10/judge-sentenced-russell-brand-praised-rape-myths-justice-bennathan"]," yesterday praised the judge in Brand’s trial for dispelling in his sentencing remarks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Suppression orders and the principles of open justice"]},{"k":"p","s":["In both the Silvagni and Carr cases, the men involved had been granted suppression orders that prevented media identifying them before they were convicted."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Age","https://www.theage.com.au/national/victoria/everybody-hates-you-every-single-day-why-the-silvagni-case-is-the-tip-of-the-iceberg-20260302-p5o6mg.html"],", the ",["Herald Sun","https://www.heraldsun.com.au/news/victoria/justin-quill-how-the-rich-like-tom-silvagni-exploit-a-legal-loophole-to-buy-court-secrecy/news-story/0bd936c84e4d3ef3ce4647c23b0836eb"],", ",["The Guardian","https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2026/jul/31/melbourne-businessman-guilty-rape-identity-suppression-gag-order-open-justice-ntwnfb"],", ",["The Australian","https://www.theaustralian.com.au/subscribe/news/1/?sourceCode=TAWEB_WRE170_a_GGL&dest=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.theaustralian.com.au%2Fcommentary%2Feditorials%2Fkeeping-secrets-a-bad-thing-for-our-open-society%2Fnews-story%2F3abd45ffd480e2ba633f5433802ec04a&memtype=anonymous&mode=premium&v21=HIGH-Segment-2-SCORE&V21spcbehaviour=appendend"]," and the ",["ABC","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-03/victoria-media-suppression-orders-court-reporting/106406950"]," all published editorials or opinion pieces on the principles of open justice and how suppression orders prevented journalists reporting on the functioning of criminal courts, an essential component of journalists’ role of keeping the public informed about the functions of a democratic society."]},{"k":"p","s":["The media cannot claim to be serving the principles of open justice and ride a wave of their own self-righteous anger at suppression orders when those orders do not prevent them covering the trial. Particularly when they are failing to cover so many trials that do not feature a well-known perpetrator."]},{"k":"p","s":["The celebrity is not the story. The rape is the story. The victim survivor and the effect he had on her life is the story. The structures that allowed him to commit his crimes can be the story, but breathless sensationalism has no place in reporting on rape."]}],"chars":4532},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"b2e4326c532e45099918e3c5d1463b779ac413a2233983e88178cfe2dbea38cd","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/chile","bytes":86209,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Chile travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T15:05:46+00:00","mod":"2026-11-09T12:06:58+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice page also covers Rapa Nui (Easter Island)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. If you have onward travel plans within the region, check travel advice for all destinations you plan to travel through. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Chile’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Chile set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Chilean Embassy in the UK","https://www.chile.gob.cl/reino-unido/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ after the day you plan to leave Chile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["British-Chilean dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["British-Chilean dual nationals must enter and leave Chile using their Chilean passport. Chilean entry and exit requirements for dual nationals may change without notice. For further information check with the ",["Chilean Embassy in the UK","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/reino-unido/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Chile for up to 90 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Chilean immigration authorities will give you a tourist card (‘tarjeta de turismo’), an A5-sized white form. Keep it safe and give it to immigration when you leave the country. If you lose it, Chilean police investigations (PDI) allows you to ",["request a copy online","https://pdivirtual.cerofilas.gob.cl/etapas/ver/31401667/0"]," (choose ‘Duplicado de tarjeta de turismo’). You can also go to the nearest PDI office."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer (to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons), you must ",["meet the Chilean Government’s entry requirements","https://serviciomigraciones.cl/en/home/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chile requires children travelling with only one parent, with a guardian or alone, to have permission from the non-travelling parent or parents. Parents travelling with children for tourism have faced difficulty leaving Chile at the end of their visit when only one parent is present. You must have"]},{"k":"li","s":["a written notarised authorisation from the non-travelling parent(s)"]},{"k":"li","s":["an original birth certificate"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling with children aged 17 and under, check the website of the ",["Chilean Ministry of Foreign Affairs","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/chile/xplica/ingreso-y-salida-de-menores-del-pais"]," (website in Spanish) for what documents you need to show."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling with dual national children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before a dual national child aged 17 or under leaves Chile, you must get authorisation to travel from a Chilean notary (‘notaría’) if the child is travelling:"]},{"k":"li","s":["alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["with only one parent or guardian"]},{"k":"li","s":["with friends or relatives"]},{"k":"p","s":["If a child was born in Chile, they must have a Chilean passport to leave the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling to Rapa Nui (Easter Island)"]},{"k":"p","s":["To ",["enter Rapa Nui (Easter Island)","https://www.gob.cl/rapanuiprotegida/en/requirements/"]," you must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["complete a ",["Rapa Nui entry form","https://ingresorapanui.interior.gob.cl/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a reservation registered with ",["SERNATUR, the national tourism service","https://serviciosturisticos.sernatur.cl/"]," (select region ‘Valparaiso’ and comuna ‘Rapa Nui’ to refine your search for accommodation) or an invitation letter from the provincial delegation"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Chile guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Chile","https://www.aduana.cl/aduana/site/edic/base/port/viajero_turista.html"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Chile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some individuals or groups claiming to represent the interests of indigenous communities have carried out attacks in the Araucanía, Biobío and Los Ríos regions of the country. State actors and businesses operating in these regions are the primary targets of these groups. You should exercise caution and follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Anarchist groups have also carried out attacks, mostly in the Santiago Metropolitan region. Attacks are principally aimed at causing property damage. Keep bags with you at all times, as unattended bags might be treated with suspicion by local authorities. Report any suspicious behaviour or unattended packages to local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violent protest in Santiago and other Chilean cities, particularly on Friday afternoons and evenings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even peaceful protests can become violent. The largest protests usually take place in central Santiago. Police can use tear gas and water cannons against protesters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all demonstrations. Under Chilean law, you can be deported if you’re involved in or promote violent acts that could disturb social order or the system of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nationwide protests often take place on significant dates, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["11 September (anniversary of the military coup)"]},{"k":"li","s":["29 March (Day of the Young Combatant)"]},{"k":"li","s":["1 May (Workers’ Day)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpocketing, mugging and thefts from vehicles are very common throughout Chile, including inside airports, churches, hotels and bus stations, and at viewpoints and petrol stations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is a list of scams and techniques which have been used on British Nationals in Chile, especially in central Santiago and Valparaiso:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Distraction robbery: The victim is distracted by one person while a second person steals the victim’s handbag or backpack from their chair or from under the table."]},{"k":"li","s":["Liquid spill: Liquid is ‘accidentally’ spilled on a traveller, and the scammer steals the victim’s valuables while pretending to be assisting cleaning it off."]},{"k":"li","s":["Tyre puncture: The driver pulls over owing to a punctured tyre (not knowing that their tyre has been deliberately punctured). A person then approaches the car offering to help, and distracts the driver whilst a second person steals belongings from the car."]},{"k":"li","s":["Hire cars: Hire cars are targeted and broken into whilst parked at a viewpoint, petrol station or other location. Sometimes the driver is approached and distracted by one person while belongings are stolen from the car by a second person."]},{"k":"li","s":["Airport taxi: Unlicenced taxi drivers at Santiago Airport add extra digits to the amount for the taxi journey i.e. charging 5,000,000 CLP (approx. 5,000 GBP / 5,000 USD) instead of 50,000 CLP. Others have convinced passengers to enter their pin number into a credit card reader whose display cannot be read. People have lost up to 10,000 GBP via this method."]},{"k":"li","s":["Theft of belongings at Santiago airport: This includes luggage stolen both before check-in at the airport terminal and from the baggage carousel after arrival."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxi scams at Santiago Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many foreign visitors have been scammed for large amounts of money by unlicensed taxi drivers, including in airport taxis. Well-known taxi companies can be booked via ridesharing apps. Only book and pay for official taxis from inside the airport before exiting the building."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not use any transport from inside the airport if you cannot pay for it before getting into the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to recognise official taxis","https://www.mtt.gob.cl/viaja-seguro-en-taxis.html"]," (in Spanish) and be wary of people impersonating authorised taxi drivers. There are criminals inside the airport arrival area who dress up as authorised taxi drivers, including people inside the airport arrival hall wearing official-looking lanyards and jackets, with printed price lists."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce the risk of being overcharged you can insist on paying in advance for your journey at one of the two official taxi booths in the arrivals at Santiago’s international airport, immediately after customs and just before you head through to the public area of arrivals. If one of the booths does not have a card reader available on that day, then you can go to the other booth instead."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do decide to pay in the taxi, you should insist on seeing the amount you are charged before you present your card for payment at the end of the journey. Carefully review the amount being charged on portable credit card machines before paying, including the number of zeroes shown on the screen."]},{"k":"p","s":["If a taxi takes you to an ATM to withdraw cash for payment, do not let the driver near the ATM while you use it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read information about the official transportation options at Santiago airport:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["taxis","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=taxis"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["buses","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=buses"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["transfers","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=transfer"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["car rental","https://www.nuevopudahuel.cl/fromairport?language=en&target=arriendo-vehiculos"]," (read the section ‘Vehicle crime’ below if you are planning on renting a car)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Book taxis in advance rather than hailing one from the street, especially late at night. Keep in groups and avoid walking alone late at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your valuables and passport somewhere secure, such as in a hotel safe. Bags hanging on chairs or mobile phones on tables can be targeted by thieves, who may use distraction techniques or work in pairs. Take particular care:"]},{"k":"li","s":["around tourist sites, and areas popular with tourists"]},{"k":"li","s":["in cafes and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["at transport hubs, including at the airport, bus stations and ports"]},{"k":"li","s":["in hotel lobbies during arrival and departure"]},{"k":"li","s":["in service (petrol) stations and service station restaurants"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling by bus or coach, take care of your belongings when getting on and off. Keep your valuables with you, do not put them in storage compartments, especially for long journeys between regions. Be extremely wary of distractions at bus stations, where there are frequent thefts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent theft (muggings)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Muggings happen frequently, especially in Santiago and Valparaiso, and increasingly with weapons such as guns and knives. Muggings can take place during the day and in plain sight of others. Be aware of your surroundings, particularly in tourist areas or near official buildings. Muggers will target:"]},{"k":"li","s":["tourists"]},{"k":"li","s":["people carrying large amounts of money – leaving ATMs or currency exchanges, for example"]},{"k":"li","s":["your passport (carrying a photocopy is enough)"]},{"k":"li","s":["valuable watches or jewellery"]},{"k":"li","s":["your mobile phone"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not resist any attempted mugging."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in criminals:"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting rental cars in major cities – they puncture the car’s tyres, often while at traffic lights, distract the occupants when they notice the tyres and steal valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["following people from the airport on arrival and robbing them, sometimes at gunpoint"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting vehicles entering or leaving private residences while the gates are opening or closing"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying out carjacking’s in Santiago, especially in affluent areas – some armed carjackers target high-end vehicles on highways"]},{"k":"li","s":["targeting people parked at viewpoints and stealing belongings from their cars"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings in and around the airport, when driving and on arrival at your destination. Keep vehicle doors locked and windows closed. Wait for gates to fully close before leaving your vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re robbed, hand over your cash and valuables without resistance. If you’re carjacked, local authorities say it is best to raise your hands and get out of the vehicle to avoid violence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink spiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["People have been given ‘spiked’ drinks in nightclubs and bars, particularly in the Suecia and Bellavista areas of Santiago. These incidents leave victims open to theft or assault. Keep your drinks in sight and be wary of people offering to buy drinks for you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry a printed copy of the photo page of your passport with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drink alcohol in public places including streets, roads, squares and promenades."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Using or possessing drugs is illegal and can lead to prison sentences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex relationships are legal in Chile and are increasingly widely accepted socially, although much of Chilean society is conservative."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Fires in national parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Open fires are illegal in national parks in Chile, outside permitted camping areas. Local authorities may revoke your tourist permit if you’re caught starting a fire in a Chilean national park. You may be asked to leave the country voluntarily within 72 hours or face deportation. If your open fire starts a larger forest fire, you may also face criminal penalties and fines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to go exploring or mountaineering, tell the local authorities before you set off. For further information on mountaineering, contact the ",["Federación de Andinismo de Chile","https://marmolejo.feach.cl/"],". For any other type of exploring, contact the ",["Chilean Embassy in London","https://www.chile.gob.cl/en/reino-unido/en"]," to see if you need a permit. The rescue services in Chile are good, but you may have to pay if they help you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Chile for 3 months. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have your passport and proof of your tourist status, such as your tourist card (‘tarjeta de turismo’) or the entry stamp in your passport, with you in the vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information about driving licences in Chile","https://www.transporteinforma.cl/atencion-de-usuarios/preguntas-frecuentes/preguntas-licencias-de-conducir/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you hire a car, get appropriate insurance. Windscreen repair can be expensive, so consider including windscreen damage cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot get car insurance if you’re driving on Rapa Nui (Easter Island). If you have an accident or do any damage to your vehicle there, you’ll have to pay for the repairs yourself."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Main roads in Chile are surfaced, but you may need a 4-wheel drive vehicle in the countryside. Be prepared for a range of driving conditions, from snow and ice to hot sandy deserts. Between June and September, winter weather sometimes temporarily closes the Chile-Argentina border crossing high in the Andes, including the main Los Libertadores crossing between Santiago and Mendoza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Toll roads are increasingly common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmine accidents mainly affect livestock and local people crossing borders at unauthorised points. Most minefields are near the borders with Peru and Bolivia in the extreme north of Chile (regions XV, I and II) and Argentina in the south (region XII). Although most minefields are clearly marked, some signs and fences are old and damaged and may be hard to spot. In some cases, minefields are laid right up to the edge of highways. Check with local authorities before travelling to more rural areas, stick to clearly marked roads and observe all warning signs."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for information about how to prepare, and how to react if there is a warning."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Heavy rain and flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["When necessary, the Chilean National Service for Disaster Prevention and Response (SENAPRED) issues warnings for heavy rain which may impact travel plans. Road conditions may be hazardous, with increased risk of delays and accidents. If you travel, plan your journey carefully and allow extra time. Follow local news, weather updates and the ",["SENAPRED website","https://senapred.cl/informate/eventos"]," (in Spanish) for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chile often has severe forest fires which can be very destructive and spread rapidly. These fires have caused multiple deaths, as well as sometimes causing the closure of national parks and roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you find yourself in or near the affected areas of any fires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities, including evacuation orders"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media to stay informed of the rapidly evolving situation"]},{"k":"li","s":["notify friends and family of your safety"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your personal security plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["make evacuation plans that do not rely on British government assistance"]},{"k":"li","s":["have travel documents up to date and easily accessible"]},{"k":"li","s":["carry identification at all times, such as your passport or a copy of it"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Major earthquakes are a risk in Chile. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],". Take note of instructions in hotel rooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["Building regulations require new structures to take account of earthquake risks. Safety measures are widely known and put into practice by national organisations and the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["A chain of volcanoes is active in the Puyehue and Los Lagos region (500 miles south of Santiago). There is a continuing risk of eruptions in Chaiten in southern Chile, Llaima in the Conguillo National Park and Lascar in northern Chile. Copahue, a volcano on the Argentina-Chile border, erupts periodically, causing local residents to be evacuated. Villarrica, a volcano near the popular tourist destinations of Pucon and Villarrica in the IX region of La Araucanía, is also active."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to these areas, monitor local media reports and follow ",["local authority volcano monitoring advice","https://www.sernageomin.cl/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Chile. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Araucanía Region"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is ongoing civil unrest in the Araucanía Region, especially around Temuco. This includes attacks by groups of demonstrators against both people and property. Be cautious if you travel within the Araucanía Region. There is an ongoing state of emergency in the provinces of Biobío, Arauco, Cautín and Malleco because of a significant increase in violent incidents. The military are assisting regional police. Follow the instructions of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 131 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["recommended vaccinations for Chile","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," or ",["Easter Island","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/69/chile-easter-island#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Chile","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile"],", including altitude sickness, which is a risk in parts of Chile. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are confirmed cases of dengue fever on Rapa Nui (Easter Island). Take steps to avoid being bitten by mosquitoes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hantavirus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hantavirus is present in Chile. Read more information about ",["Hantavirus in Chile on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/48/chile#Outbreaks"],". Further guidance on Hantavirus is available from the ",["UK Health Security Agency","https://ukhsa.blog.gov.uk/2026/05/05/what-is-hantavirus-how-is-it-transmitted-and-what-are-the-symptoms/"]," and ",["Chile’s Ministry of Health","https://www.minsal.cl/ministerio-de-salud-declara-alerta-sanitaria-por-hantavirus-desde-atacama-a-magallanes/"]," (website in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are good health facilities in Santiago and other major cities, but private clinics and hospitals are expensive. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is only one hospital on Rapa Nui (Easter Island) and its facilities are limited. People suffering from serious illnesses or injuries are taken by air ambulance to mainland Chile for treatment. Make sure your travel insurance covers this."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-2"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-chile-guidance"]," if you’re living in Chile."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Chile"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 131"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 132"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 133"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Chile"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Chile"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Chile"]," in Chile"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/chile-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/chile/british-embassy-santiago"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/chile/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Chile","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-chile"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":22722,"change":"Removal of information about heavy rain and severe mudslides in eastern Santiago ('Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"f6e863996b102882d47309753f994dd3e3ea490af897b0e312efcc6bbe36ba8b","read":"https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-peace-deal-is-unravelling-what-went-wrong-with-the-tigray-agreement-293005","bytes":184342,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Ethiopia’s peace deal is unravelling – what went wrong with the Tigray agreement","by":[{"n":"Alemayehu Fentaw Weldemariam","r":"Ph.D. Fellow, Center for Constitutional Democracy, Indiana University"}],"pub":"2026-09-29T08:37:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria peace deal","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," in Ethiopia was an agreement to cease hostilities. It wasn’t a comprehensive political settlement. A ",["political settlement","https://doi.org/10.1093/oso/9780192848932.003.0002"]," is an enduring agreement among powerful groups that delivers some benefits to avert conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ethiopian government and the Tigray People’s Liberation Front signed the Pretoria agreement in 2022. It ",["stopped large-scale fighting","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-tigray-war-parties-agree-pause-expert-insights-into-two-years-of-devastating-conflict-193636"]," in Tigray and created a framework for disarmament and other immediate measures. But it was also meant to pave the way for political dialogue addressing underlying disputes."]},{"k":"p","s":["This political settlement would have restored Tigray’s self-rule through an elected regional government. It would have restored the region’s representation in ",["Ethiopia’s two houses of parliament","https://theconversation.com/what-is-federalism-why-ethiopia-uses-this-system-of-government-and-why-its-not-perfect-217217"],", and the federal executive and judiciary. Instead, the Tigray People’s Liberation Front was ",["deregistered and Tigray was excluded","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn0pngz2rego"]," from the June 2026 elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria deal","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," also required the withdrawal of Eritrean and other non-federal forces from Tigrayan territories. It called for accountability for alleged war crimes and other violations."]},{"k":"p","s":["This broader settlement was never reached. The ",["consequences","https://acleddata.com/expert-comment/ethiopia-conflict-expert-insights"]," are now becoming clear."]},{"k":"p","s":["Fighting has ",["resumed","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/26/is-ethiopia-on-the-verge-of-another-civil-war-as-fighting-erupts-in-tigray"]," between government troops and Tigrayan forces, with air and drone strikes hitting the region. Seven armed organisations – including groups that fought one another during the ",["2020-2022 Tigray war","https://www.cfr.org/global-conflict-tracker/conflict/conflict-ethiopia"]," – have formed an ",["alliance","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/seven-ethiopian-armed-groups-announce-anti-government-alliance-2026-09-21/"]," seeking to remove Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed’s government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the international response to the escalation in conflict has focused on the ",["Tigray People’s Liberation Front","https://www.britannica.com/place/Tigray-historical-region-Ethiopia#ref248314"],". In late September 2026, for instance, US ambassador Ervin Massinga ",["accused","https://et.usembassy.gov/statement-on-recent-developments-in-tigray-and-afar/"]," the front of making the"]},{"k":"p","s":["poor decision to launch a large-scale offensive."]},{"k":"p","s":["He described the campaign as an “ ",["unwinnable fight","https://et.usembassy.gov/statement-on-recent-developments-in-tigray-and-afar/"],"”, and threatened further sanctions against the front and leaders of the newly formed armed alliance."]},{"k":"p","s":["But focusing on who launched the latest offensive risks obscuring a more important question: why the ",["peace process","https://theconversation.com/ethiopia-tigray-war-parties-agree-pause-expert-insights-into-two-years-of-devastating-conflict-193636"]," that ended the Tigray war in 2022 failed to prevent a return to conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a ",["constitutional scholar and country expert","https://scholar.google.com/citations?hl=en&user=arlPf30AAAAJ&view_op=list_works&sortby=pubdate"]," on Ethiopia, whose focus includes peacemaking and peacebuilding. In my view, the failure to move from the Pretoria agreement to a broader political settlement has had three major consequences:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the emergence of an armed alliance connecting conflicts across several regions"]},{"k":"li","s":["renewed attacks that risk further civilian casualties and mass displacement"]},{"k":"li","s":["growing tensions with Eritrea that could draw Ethiopia’s conflicts into a wider regional confrontation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing a broader war in Ethiopia will, therefore, require more than a return to the Pretoria agreement. The country needs a comprehensive political settlement. This should be negotiated between Abiy’s leadership and anti-government forces – not just another bilateral agreement with Tigray."]},{"k":"h","s":["The transition"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Pretoria agreement","https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/cessation-of-hostilities-agreement-between-the-government-of-the-federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia-and-the-tigray-peoples-liberation-front-tplf"]," imposed military and political obligations on both the Ethiopian government and Tigrayan forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Tigray People’s Liberation Front was to disarm. The federal government was to help remove the front’s terrorist designation, restore essential services in Tigray and enable humanitarian access. Federal authority was to return to Tigray."]},{"k":"p","s":["Subsequent ",["peace talks in Nairobi","https://www.peaceagreements.org/media/documents/ag2464_6391cad1825da.pdf"]," linked the handover of Tigray’s heavy weapons to the withdrawal of foreign and non-federal forces from Tigray."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Ethiopia’s troubled history provides clues to why an all-out civil war is possible","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-troubled-history-provides-clues-to-why-an-all-out-civil-war-is-possible-149648"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Tigrayan forces began surrendering heavy weapons in January 2023. An African Union monitoring team ",["witnessed and confirmed","https://apnews.com/article/2214ccbe43c96047f9f8f9465da9a988"]," this process. But the federal government did not secure the corresponding withdrawal of forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["These failures don’t absolve Tigray’s leadership of some responsibility for the escalation in conflict. Its restoration of the ",["pre-war regional administration","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/tigray-party-restores-pre-war-government-threat-northern-ethiopia-peace-2026-05-05/"]," went against the Pretoria agreement, which provided for an interim administration established through dialogue. It would govern until elections could be held under the supervision of the National Election Board. Further, reports of ",["forced military mobilisation","https://www.hrw.org/news/2026/07/06/ethiopia-tigray-authorities-forcibly-recruiting-civilians"]," are serious."]},{"k":"p","s":["But these actions occurred within a peace process already weakened by incomplete implementation."]},{"k":"h","s":["The consequences"]},{"k":"p","s":["The formation of an ",["anti-government coalition","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/ckp84pj8zpngo"]," changes the environment. The Ethiopian Peoples’ Forces Alliance for Survival includes the Tigray People’s Liberation Front, the Oromo Liberation Army, Amhara Fano elements and organisations from other regions. Some of these groups previously fought one another."]},{"k":"p","s":["The alliance doesn’t mean Abiy’s government is about to collapse. The federal state ",["retains","https://www.theafricareport.com/431885/can-abiys-drones-give-him-the-upper-hand-in-ethiopias-full-blown-war/"]," the army, air power, drones, federal revenues and the machinery of government."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the alliance doesn’t need a common ideology or unified battlefield command to create problems for the federal government. Coordination of operations across regions could be enough."]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in Tigray could draw federal forces northward. Fighting in ",["Amhara","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-amhara-people-are-being-portrayed-as-the-enemy-the-dangerous-history-of-ethnic-politics-212626"]," might absorb forces and obstruct access to the north. Pressure in ",["Oromia","https://theconversation.com/ethiopias-other-conflict-whats-driving-the-violence-in-oromia-187035"]," might require the government to defend approaches to the capital and major transport corridors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Each front can, therefore, affect the others even if the alliance’s forces never fight side by side."]},{"k":"p","s":["The immediate challenge for the federal government is the dispersion of forces across distant conflicts with different terrain, supply lines and political dynamics."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Renewed air and drone attacks","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cry8zwwq21pxo"]," raise the danger of another humanitarian crisis, too. Tigray is ",["still recovering","https://theconversation.com/starvation-as-a-weapon-of-war-how-ethiopia-created-a-famine-in-tigray-268395"]," from the 2020-2022 war. Escalation risks civilian casualties, displacement and disruption to humanitarian assistance."]},{"k":"h","s":["The Eritrea and Sudan question"]},{"k":"p","s":["Eritrea’s role in the latest escalation in conflict remains disputed. Ethiopia ",["accuses","https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/ethiopia-accuses-eritrea-military-aggression-backing-armed-groups-2026-02-08/"]," Asmara of supporting armed groups. Eritrea ",["denies","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn87lzrj1l7o"]," it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Abiy and other senior Ethiopian officials have also repeatedly said they must have ",["access to the Red Sea","https://adf-magazine.com/2026/02/eritrea-ethiopia-port-dispute-heats-up/"],". Talk of the ",["Eritrean port of Assab","https://www.dw.com/en/port-assab-becomes-flashpoint-for-ethiopiaeritrea-relations/a-75453946"]," has been understood in Eritrea as a threat. Assab is part of Eritrea’s internationally recognised territory. Any attempt to acquire it by force would violate Eritrean sovereignty."]},{"k":"p","s":["The conflict could also become entangled with Sudan’s war. According to a ",["Reuters report","https://www.reuters.com/investigations/ethiopia-builds-secret-camp-train-sudan-rsf-fighters-sources-say-2026-02-10/"],", Ethiopia hosts a camp used to train paramilitary fighters for Sudan’s Rapid Support Forces. Ethiopia has denied involvement. It instead accuses Sudan’s armed forces of ",["supporting","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/28/ethiopia-accuses-sudan-egypt-of-backing-tigray-rebels-as-fighting-rages"]," the Tigray People’s Liberation Front. Sudan ",["denies","https://addisstandard.com/sudan-army-rejects-ethiopias-claims-of-backing-armed-opposition-coalition/"]," this."]},{"k":"p","s":["If these alignments harden, the Ethiopian and Sudanese conflicts could provide one another with weapons supply routes. They could also supply recruits, rear bases and external support. This raises the risk of conflict extending from Sudan through northern Ethiopia towards Eritrea and the Red Sea."]},{"k":"h","s":["What next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The immediate priorities are ending attacks on populated areas and protecting humanitarian corridors. Independent monitoring must also be restored and outstanding security obligations completed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another bilateral bargain between Addis Ababa and the Tigray People’s Liberation Front would be inadequate. The conflict now connects armed movements and political grievances across several regions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Preventing a wider war requires a comprehensive agreement that involves the federal government, the alliance of armed groups, non-armed political actors and civil society. It must address territorial disputes, political representation, elections, accountability, regional autonomy, constitutional reform and the distribution of power."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pretoria stopped one phase of one war. Its incomplete implementation left unresolved disputes that are now colliding."]}],"chars":7600},"https://theconversation.com/international-surrogacy-and-the-narrow-legal-idea-of-what-makes-a-family-legitimate-295302":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"bf0648582d32fc9ee87497d9c1ba048815e1e5bc153454c19a2c4a2f6023657c","read":"https://theconversation.com/international-surrogacy-and-the-narrow-legal-idea-of-what-makes-a-family-legitimate-295302","bytes":179481,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"International surrogacy and the narrow legal idea of what makes a family legitimate","by":[{"n":"Katie Tonkiss","r":"Senior Lecturer in Sociology, Aston University"}],"pub":"2026-11-04T14:37:12Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["A recent family court judgment in the UK highlighted ethical issues with the practice of international surrogacy. The case is thought to be the first to come before a court in the UK involving a surrogate who gave birth in China, where surrogacy is illegal. It raised numerous concerns – including about the welfare of the surrogate and child, the use of sex selection and the child’s immigration status and nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Surrogacy","https://theconversation.com/topics/surrogacy-4090"]," is a growing practice in the UK, with the number of ",["births doubling","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/19/rise-overseas-surrogates-increases-risk-stateless-babies-experts-warn"]," between 2015 and 2025. Most of these babies are born overseas through ",["international surrogacy","https://www.ngalaw.co.uk/numbers-talk-our-scope-of-surrogacy"],". In the UK, surrogacy is permitted only under altruistic circumstances (such as a relative or friend of the intended parents carrying the baby, with no payment beyond expenses). This can make it difficult to find a domestic surrogate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Domestic surrogacy ",["is prohibited","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2025/769508/EPRS_BRI(2025)769508_EN.pdf"]," across all EU member nations. But in countries such as Georgia, Ukraine and many states in the US, commercial surrogacy – where the surrogate receives payment over and above her expenses – is legal. An industry has grown around the practice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on their place of birth, babies born through international surrogacy can enter a legal grey area where their nationality is uncertain. In some cases, this can lead to the risk of statelessness because of discrepancies in how legal parenthood – and therefore often nationality – are recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Where commercial surrogacy is legal, a surrogate may not be recognised as having legal parenthood of a child at all. But when a family seeks to return to their country of residence with the child, if surrogacy is not legal in that country, then the legal parenthood of the “intended parents” may also not be recognised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Given that legal parenthood determines nationality in most countries, this can leave children born through surrogacy without a clear claim to nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["the case","https://caselaw.nationalarchives.gov.uk/ewfc/2026/279"]," of the baby born in China, it was not until the child was 20 months old that the parenthood of the “intended parents”, and therefore the child’s British nationality, was established in law."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attempts to increase regulation of surrogacy internationally ",["have stalled","https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/jul/19/rise-overseas-surrogates-increases-risk-stateless-babies-experts-warn"]," because of disagreement between states over the ethical issues raised by the practice. But having no nationality, as can arise in international surrogacy, also calls into question the foundations upon which access to legal identity at birth is built."]},{"k":"p","s":["For my ",["new book","https://manchesteruniversitypress.co.uk/9781526183514/"],", I researched cases of international surrogacy across Europe and North America, speaking to parents as well as surrogates. I found that ideas about what counts as a “legitimate” family shape decisions about what citizenship, if any, a child should have at birth."]},{"k":"h","s":["What is a ‘legitimate’ family?"]},{"k":"p","s":["The idea of “legitimate” and “illegitimate” families has become almost obsolete in other areas of the law. But it persists when it comes to establishing nationality."]},{"k":"p","s":["In European countries, nationality at birth is decided by the parent or parents’ nationality. The child effectively inherits it from the parents. A number of ",["high-profile cases","https://www.echr.coe.int/documents/d/echr/fs_surrogacy_eng"]," before the European Court of Human Rights have sought to ensure that no child born through surrogacy could be rendered stateless, despite the prohibition of the practice across EU member states."]},{"k":"p","s":["But I found that despite this, decisions about legal parenthood – and therefore nationality – continue to be shaped by gendered assumptions about what counts as parenthood. Specifically, the need for a gestating mother and a father who is biologically related to the child is central. I also found that, even where countries have laws to protect children born through surrogacy, LGBTQ+ parents may face obstacles in registering births, because of the absence of a gestational mother in the paperwork."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the US, nationality typically is decided by birth on US soil. However, in cases of international surrogacy – where the child is born overseas – a child may inherit their citizenship from a parent who is a US citizen."]},{"k":"p","s":["A series of ",["cases","https://immigrationequality.org/andrew-elad-and-ethan-dvash-banks/"]," before the US Supreme Court showed how stricter standards were applied to the children of LGBTQ+ couples born through international surrogacy. They were assumed to be born “out of wedlock”, despite their parents being married."]},{"k":"p","s":["These children struggled to obtain US nationality as a result. The court ruled to prevent this discrimination, but this work has reinforced the importance of marriage to parenthood. That is, it focused on the legitimacy of the marriages, rather than the relevance of marriage to parenthood."]},{"k":"p","s":["While ethical debates around surrogacy are unlikely to be resolved any time soon, children continue to face the risk of statelessness."]},{"k":"p","s":["States that oppose surrogacy argue that strict rules are needed to prevent exploitation, the commodification of children and human trafficking. These concerns are very real. Yet growing numbers of children are being born through international surrogacy and face the risk of statelessness."]},{"k":"p","s":["Addressing this requires not only renewed efforts at regulation, but also a fundamental rethink of nationality laws. So often, these tie a child’s legal identity to narrow ideas of what counts as a “legitimate” family."]}],"chars":5138}};
